hundreds of thousands of Muslim devotees  from all walks of life from all around  the world have gathered in Bangladesh  for three days of prayers and sermons  bisho istama or Global Congregation of  Muslims held each year since 1967 aims  to revive the tenets of Islam and  promote peace  I along with hundreds of others came all  the way from Palestine on a long journey  to learn more about the essence of Islam  and its teachings  the estimate is considered an expression  of Muslim Unity solidarity love and  respect  we came here to learn the meaning of  life about why we were born we all have  to return to Allah we have to understand  all these teachings of our prophet and  the Quran we can't learn these things by  staying home we have to travel  Muslim devotees spent three days crammed  into tents in five square kilometer area  those who couldn't find Space on istama  ground camped on the footpaths  we have heard so much about the large  ichima gatherings in Bangladesh now we  are very happy to be here and  participate in this auspicious religious  gathering the large number of worshipers  is a challenge for authorities there's a  strong security presence and Healthcare  and other basic services are provided  this is a very large Gathering of people  from everywhere it can be difficult but  people are in a good mood and smiling  we're here to please Allah so it's not a  hardship for us  it is estimated that more than 3 million  devotees took part this year the first  phase of one of the largest Muslim  gatherings in the world is to end this  Sunday with hundreds of thousands of  muslims praying for Global Peace divine  blessing and the Revival of Islamic  valuesipur
 

